# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — the part no language template can know about
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `masterlinker setup` writes both of these into the working directory, which
# for most people is this clone. The config holds a Zello account password; the
# key is an RSA private key from the developer console. Never commit either.
# If you already have, revoke the key at developers.zello.com before anything
# else — deleting the commit is not enough once it has been pushed.
masterlinker.json
masterlinker.*.json
!config.example.json
*.key
*.pem

# The CLI reads MASTERLINKER_USER and MASTERLINKER_PASSWORD from the
# environment, so a .env file here would hold your panel login.
.env
.envrc

# PyPI upload credentials
.pypirc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
shots/
*.log
*.pid

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so

# Environments
venv/
.venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# Packaging and build
.Python
build/
dist/
sdist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
develop-eggs/
parts/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
MANIFEST
# Note: GitHub's template also lists lib/ and lib64/ here. They are omitted on
# purpose — nothing in this project builds into them, and silently ignoring a
# source directory someone names lib/ is the likelier accident.

# PyInstaller, if anyone packages this as a Windows executable
*.manifest
*.spec

